{"id": "EUVD-2026-83284", "enisaUuid": "f469c7c8-07e5-3a30-9048-d9dfe2ae1705", "description": "vLLM before 0.29.0 validates allowed_token_ids against tokenizer length instead of model output logits width in SamplingParams._validate_allowed_token_ids(). Attackers can supply token IDs above the output vocabulary that pass validation, causing LogitBiasState to corrupt GPU logits state and allow concurrent requests to sample tokens outside their allowlists.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T19:06:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:23:15", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49080", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/5b0e5b69ac1a3884a6479c9537789c95263cc804", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.28.0/vllm/sampling_params.py#L881-L903", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.28.0/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/logit_bias.py#L179-L191", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-before-0.29.0-cross-request-logits-corruption-via-allowed-token-ids"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-3998", "GHSA-97fp-7cr2-23qc", "CVE-2026-93840"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f3641acf-d48b-312e-bff6-681ba9943cce", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.29.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0ec0fa73-4464-366b-9d1a-585e89a95bed", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}